  "worked_solution": "The product rule and the addition rule for derivatives give\n\n$$\n{h}^{\u2032}(x)={f}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot g(x)+f(x)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{\u2032}(-2)={f}^{\u2032}(-2)\\cdot g(-2)+f(-2)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(-2).\n$$\n\nFrom the graphs above, we obtain that $f(-2)=0$ and $g(-2)=3.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (-4,0)$ equals $-1.$ So, ${f}^{\u2032}(-2)=-1.$\n\n- The slope of $g(x)$ on $x\\in (-4,0)$ equals $\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, ${g}^{\u2032}(-2)=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{\u2032}(-2) & ={f}^{\u2032}(-2)\\cdot g(-2)+f(-2)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(-2)-{f}^{\u2032}(-2) \\\\  & =-1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
